  "id": "COMPOUND:757 - PROTEIN:5338",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that etoposide may be associated with C32 through multiple, albeit distinct, pathways. The first pathway links etoposide to Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and ultimately to C32. The second and third pathways connect etoposide to palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets C32 through P2X purinoceptor 7. These pathways involve different molecular mechanisms, yet they all converge on C32 as a downstream target. The presence of multiple targets and their respective mechanisms indicates a complex, possibly redundant, network of interactions. The integration of these pathways suggests that etoposide may exert its effects on C32 through diverse molecular mechanisms, potentially involving both direct and indirect interactions. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between etoposide and C32, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
